      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(browser): prove post-action target continuity before adopting a tab",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nAfter a browser navigation or action invalidates the selected raw target, route code retried tab lists and adopted replacements via heuristics: any sole remaining tab, a uniquely new post-action tab, or a uniquely URL-matching tab. None of those prove the acted-on page identity, so `/act` could return an unrelated tab's `targetId` and silently redirect the caller's next mutating action onto the wrong page.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nClawSweeper's recommended path for the route-safety fix: make each backend return its operation-owned target outcome; remove route-level list inference entirely. Playwright navigate/act now read the acted-on page's raw target id via `Target.getTargetInfo` after the operation and return it on the result. Routes apply `resolveOperationTargetOutcome`: backend-reported id when present, otherwise the acted-on id (stale/closed) so callers require a fresh selection.\n\nRemoved heuristics:\n- adopting a uniquely new post-action tab\n- adopting a uniquely URL-matching tab (renderer swap inferred from lists)\n- sole remaining tab fallback\n\n**Fail-safe recovery contract (intentional):** when a backend cannot prove post-action target continuity, routes return the stale acted-on `targetId` instead of inferring a surviving unrelated tab. Callers that need to continue must re-select from a fresh tab list. This trades heuristic continuation for wrong-tab safety (#103785).\n\nExtension-relay profiles use the same Playwright `readPageTargetId` backend for navigate/act outcomes (no route-level list inference). Chrome MCP existing-session uses tab-list membership via `readChromeMcpOperationTargetId` after navigate/act; close reports `operationTargetId: null`.\n\n**Deferred (separate browser-contract PR):** extension-relay opaque public CDP target handles (`openclaw-relay-<nonce>-<ordinal>`) and relay-bridge identity migration. This PR intentionally does not change `relay-bridge.ts` public target IDs so route safety can land without a compatibility-sensitive relay contract decision.\n\n## User Impact\n\n- **Playwright navigate/act:** response `targetId` is the backend-owned identity of the page that executed the operation. If the page closes, the acted-on id is returned (stale) and callers must re-select.\n- **Extension-relay /navigate and /act:** route applies `resolveOperationTargetOutcome` to `readPageTargetId` outcomes (no list inference). Relay CDP public target IDs are unchanged from current main.\n- **Chrome MCP existing-session /act:** route applies `resolveOperationTargetOutcome` to tab-list membership; stale acted-on id preserved when the tab is gone.\n- **No wrong-tab routing:** unrelated tabs left open are never adopted from tab lists, URL cardinality, or sole-tab fallback.\n- **Continuity preserved:** renderer swaps and action-triggered replacements still work when the backend reports the new raw target id (#25323 / #25326 / #46137).\n\n## Evidence\n\nHead: `aa12f719135` (rebased onto `main` @ `9d2f5d4dbb63`, current with main, 2026-07-19)\n\n### Live browser proof (real Chrome/CDP, route-level contracts)\n\nHarness: `extensions/browser/scripts/proof-103785-target-continuity.test-harness.mts`\n\nRun:\n\n```\npnpm exec tsx extensions/browser/scripts/proof-103785-target-continuity.test-harness.mts\n```\n\nRedacted output (fresh run on rebased head):\n\n```\n=== Live-browser proof for #103785 (backend-owned page identity) ===\n\nScenario A: action closes acted-on tab A; unrelated tab B survives\n  kept acted-on identity A: true\n  adopted unrelated survivor B: false\n  PASS: unrelated survivor B was NOT adopted.\n\nScenario B: renderer swap (page reattaches under new raw target at navigated url)\n  adopted backend-reported reattached target: true\n  PASS: renderer-swap continuity preserved.\n\nScenario C: extension-relay /navigate route (readPageTargetId post-navigate + route resolver)\n  readPageTargetId (navigateViaPlaywright return contract)=C244AB73… url=http://[redacted-host]/…\n  /navigate route outcome target=C244AB73… (acted-on=C244AB73…)\n  adopted backend-reported post-navigate target: true\n  PASS: extension-relay route preserved backend-owned identity.\n\nScenario D: Chrome MCP existing-session /act route (tab-list membership + resolver)\n  D1 tab still in list: kept acted-on identity when tab survives: true\n  D2 tab gone after close: stale acted-on id preserved when tab is gone: true\n  PASS: Chrome MCP route contract honored for survive + close.\n\n=== ALL SCENARIOS PASSED ===\n```\n\nScenario C exercises the extension-relay route resolver over real Chrome via Playwright `readPageTargetId` (the same backend path extension-relay profiles use). It does not change relay-bridge public CDP target IDs.\n\n### Deferred relay public-ID migration\n\nFollow-up work (not in this PR): instance-scoped opaque relay handles, bridge regressions, and live paired Chrome extension proof for detach/reattach continuity. Requires `@steipete` browser-contract approval before landing.\n\n### Source and test changes\n\n- `resolveOperationTargetOutcome` replaces list-inference resolver; no tab-list adoption.\n- `readPageTargetId` exported from Playwright session; `navigateViaPlaywright` and `executeActViaPlaywright` return `targetId`.\n- `readChromeMcpOperationTargetId` exported; Chrome MCP existing-session `/act` and close wire operation-owned outcomes.\n- Extension-relay `/navigate` and Playwright `/act` paths wire backend outcomes via `resolveOperationTargetOutcome`.\n- `relay-bridge.ts` unchanged from main (relay public-ID migration deferred).\n- Route-level `/act` regression: stale acted-on id when backend reports no operation-owned target.\n- Sole-survivor resolver regression: Chrome MCP tab-list membership never adopts unrelated survivor.\n\nAutomated tests:\n\n```\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/browser/src/browser/routes/agent.snapshot.test.ts extensions/browser/src/browser/server.agent-contract-core.test.ts extensions/browser/src/browser/extension-relay/relay-bridge.test.ts\n# 47 passed\n```\n\nExtension package boundary typecheck: `extension package boundary check passed`.\n\nCloses #103785\n",
